## VI.4 Computational structure

1. **Simulate once.** The engine produces, per owner, the scenario matrix $M_{o,j}$ and the shared $\bar S_j$, $\bar C_j$ vectors. One simulation, all downstream uses.
2. **Per-owner program.** $J + 2$ variables and $\sim J$ constraints — milliseconds in any LP/QP solver (CLARABEL, HiGHS, Gurobi).
3. **Price sweep.** Loop the program over the premium grid — embarrassingly parallel, and fast if DPP is preserved (§V.3).
4. **Aggregate.** Horizontal sum across owners; build the retailer demand side identically.
5. **Inference offline.** Steps 11–13 run on historical AEMO and financial data, independent of the simulation, producing the $\widehat q$ actuals.
6. **Calibrate.** An outer optimisation over $\{\lambda_o, \gamma_o\}$ wrapping the sweep — a handful of iterations.

**Keep the modules separate.** They have different refresh cadences: the margin and supply views refresh with the screen; inference refreshes with each AEMO and financial data drop; calibration refreshes on a slower cycle.

## VI.5 Suggested build order

1. **SRMC and cost stack** (§I.8) — everything references it, and the two-threshold framing must be right before dispatch is written.
2. **Price simulator with joint gas**, calibrated level-then-tail (§I.9). Gate on the cap reprice check before proceeding.
3. **Non-anticipative commitment + dispatch** (§I.7), starting with the heuristic rule; upgrade to DP once the heuristic is validated against realised plant behaviour.
4. **Master margin equation and outputs** (§I.1, §I.10) — the distribution, not the mean.
5. **The minimal six dashboard charts** (§II.9). Stop here and you already have a defensible desk tool.
6. **Netted per-owner margin $M_o$** (§III.1) — the piece that inverts the answer for the largest participants. Get it right before building any supply curve on top.
7. **Per-owner mean-var-CVaR program and price sweep** (§III.5, §III.8).
8. **OI ceiling check** (§IV.14) — trivially cheap, catches errors in everything downstream.
9. **Markup inversion with the below/above split** (§IV.13), validated on synthetic planted positions first.
10. **Aggregation, demand side, clearing, implied $\lambda$** (§III.9, §III.10).
11. **Calibration loop** (§IV.15) — and take the residual seriously.

